  "source_target_review": "Manual source review of every copied C/header: services_main reaches the firmware init/pump wrappers for one static firmware_owner. Its sole initializer calls a138_business_mmio_bus and a138_record_mmio_bus; those constructors bind business_mmio_read/write and record_mmio_read/write. a138_ble_business_init copies both buses once. No source reassigns either callback field after initialization, and the service-root closure has no other bus instance. Each site conservatively includes both read/write targets for its bus type. Interrupts remain disabled. All source inputs and the exact complete disassembly are hash-bound; -fno-jump-tables is an explicit business build option. This review does not authorize arbitrary external callers or future changed inputs. Final v8 source review: a torn STALE observation stays in OBSERVE under the existing1000ms bound; only a complete context session change ends the old publication observation. This adds no callback, bus assignment, or owner entry point. All source hashes and actual machine sites have been regenerated; the same four static MMIO adapters remain the complete target closure.",
